# GD-2 (round 19): L §4.2 day_of(y, md): "Of a key of an anchored year index it is refused as `day_of(m, n)` of an
# anchored key is", at load where load sees the index (LOAD-DOMAIN, L §8.3 round 19: "`day_of` or `schedule` of a key
# of an anchored index").
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index yrs = year 2026..2027
input file_by: monthday
input other: monthday
index fy = year 2026..2027 from 04-06
def d[y in fy]: date = day_of(y, file_by)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  file_by = 04-30
  other = 04-30
ask q: d[2026]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DOMAIN day_of of a key of the anchored index fy has no meaning (m.tally:13)
